# Agent guide

**Orcan** = Docker **context orchestrator** for Cursor CLI (`agent`) and Claude Code (`claude`): workspaces, path-parity mounts, ignore/instruction seeds, browser terminal. Agent CLIs are tools inside it; **models are out of scope**.

Display name: **Orcan**. Technical ids: `orcan`, `ORCAN_*`. **Orcan** is the only product name in docs and user-facing text.

Read root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) and [`docs/en/ai/project-context.md`](../../docs/en/ai/project-context.md). This rule is always applied.

## Product ritual (host)

```bash
make config-wizard    # or setup / config-scaffold / hand-edit orcan.config.json
make env              # ALWAYS after config changes (terminal* does not call env)
make rebuild          # after Dockerfile / docker/rootfs / tmux / shell changes
make terminal-docker  # daily start (ttyd); or make terminal without Docker socket
```

Recreate after env changes: `make down && make terminal-docker`.

## Config = JSON only

- User profile: **`orcan.config.json`** (stdlib `json` — **no PyYAML**, no `host-deps`, no `requirements-host.txt`).
- Example: `orcan.config.example.json`.
- Keep Compose/docs YAML (`docker-compose*.yml`, `mkdocs.yml`, generated `.orcan/*.yml`).
- Do not revive YAML user configs.

## Runtime stack (container)

```text
ttyd (cursor-ttyd) → cursor-launcher → tmux → zsh
  Starship prompt · autosuggestions · syntax-highlighting · fzf
  aliases: /etc/orcan/shell/aliases.sh
```

| Concern | Source of truth |
| --- | --- |
| tmux | `docker/rootfs/etc/tmux/` (2-row status; RMB menus unbound in `tmux.conf`) |
| zsh | `docker/rootfs/etc/skel/.zshrc` + `.zshrc.d/` |
| git/starship seeds | `docker/rootfs/opt/orcan/` |
| Cursor defaults | `docker/rootfs/opt/cursor-defaults/` → seeded missing-only |

## File map

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `Dockerfile` | Image build |
| `docker-compose*.yml` | Runtime overlays |
| `.orcan/*` | Generated runtime (gitignored; from `make env`) |
| `Makefile` | Host UI |
| `docker/rootfs/` | Image filesystem |
| `scripts/repository/` | Host-only helpers |
| `docs/` | MkDocs (canonical docs) |
| `README.md` | Short entry only |
| `AGENTS.md` | Short agent orientation |
| `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | Rules for this repository |

## Commands (high-signal)

Configure: `make setup` · `make env` · `make config-wizard` · `make config-scaffold` · `make config-show` · `make init-project-all`

Run: `make build` · `make build-claude` · `make release` · `make terminal` · `make terminal-docker` · `make down` · `make path-check` · `make validate` · `make docs-check` · `make test` · `make help`

Claude-only: `IMAGE_LOCAL=orcan:claude make terminal-docker`.  
Release: `make bump-patch` → commit `VERSION`+`CHANGELOG.md` → `make release` (GitHub Release; no image publish).

## Boundaries

Allowed: edit this repo; Make/Compose checks; image builds; update docs when the interface changes.

Not allowed: host paths outside the project; modify `.env` unless asked; `docker system prune`; delete `ORCAN_DATA` except via explicit `make clean-data`; `--privileged`; claim build success without running the build.

## Done checklist

- [ ] `make validate` passes
- [ ] `make test-host` passes
- [ ] `make docs-check` passes when docs/interface changed
- [ ] Compose config OK
- [ ] `make help` matches real targets / docs
- [ ] No secrets in image or repo
- [ ] Report: tests ran / skipped / limits

